nsider most Linux distributions to be at-risk until patched.  Since the \u201cDirtyFrag\u201d vulnerability was disclosed prior to upstream patches having been made available, we are forced to wait for the different OS providers to create new releases or patches before we can integrate them into the versions we make available to customers.\n\nAs this is a rapidly developing incident, we will provide further information regarding recommended actions, possible mitigations, and OS updates for all customers who may be affected.\n\n[1] https://github.com/V4bel/dirtyfrag/blob/master/assets/write-up.md\n[2] https://www.linode.com/docs/guides/cve-2026-31431-copy-fail-mitigation/", "incident_id": "wsvxwlyhw1t5", "created_at": "2026-05-08T13:40:35.577Z", "updated_at": "2026-05-08T13:40:35.577Z", "display_at": "2026-05-08T13:40:35.577Z", "affected_components": [{"code": "61mfhwczrxzt", "name": "Linode Manager and API", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "mmgkdgcjgnbl", "name": "Hosted DNS Service", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "v8zpnn61fcdm", "name": "Regions - US-East (Newark)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "s8355f9s5hpx", "name": "Regions - US-Central (Dallas)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "v5mcdxdt9dtv", "name": "Regions - US-West (Fremont)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "ss2n92gy5xkk", "name": "Regions - US-Southeast (Atlanta)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "h9sk1q74fyb6", "name": "Regions - US-IAD (Washington)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "43zk807gj6fx", "name": "Regions - US-ORD (Chicago)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "ptln4fx0jhrt", "name": "Regions - CA-Central (Toronto)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "jzjmxld11n92", "name": "