erational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "8z2njrmgllxf", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - BR-GRU (S\u00e3o Paulo)  Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "60bbgt40jng1", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - NL-AMS (Amsterdam) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "vqfphnkhfkvs", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - ES-MAD (Madrid) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "mwgwvltj8ptp", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - IT-MIL (Milan) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "ylkjs26zf4td", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - US-MIA (Miami) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "jtys8n1thtpp", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - US-LAX (Los Angeles) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "9hvhx2xs22lq", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - GB-LON (London 2) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "75tt2yzzgynz", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - AU-MEL (Melbourne) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "lrjfl1pkp7v4", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - IN-BOM-2 (Mumbai 2) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "c6fx4ttdx2kf", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - DE-FRA-2 (Frankfurt 2) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "vxp9y8rmp0vh", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - SG-SIN-2 (Singapore 2) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "5bqgy49ck8pz", "name": "Linode Kubernetes Engine - JP-TYO-3 (Tokyo 3) Linode Kubernetes Engine", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}], "deliver_notifications": false, "custom_tweet": null, "tweet_id": null}, {"id": "drwkj2npjq06", "status": "investigating", "body": "Akamai is aware of the recently disclosed \u201cCopy Fail\u201d vulnerability (CVE-2026-31431). We are assessing the issue and are working to address it across our product portfolio and internal systems. While we have not observed any related malicious exploits targeting our infrastructure, Akamai continuously works to reduce risks and enhance our security posture. We are taking both immediate and longer-term steps to mitigate potential impacts and help ensure the continued confidence of our customers. \n\nPer our Shared Security Model[1], customers are responsible for making sure their service\u2019s installed applications and code are securely configured and patched. Given the nature of this vulnerability, it should be assumed that all virtual machines running Linux are at-risk until patched. We will be publishing more details as patches are incorporated into the base images that we supply, but we strongly recommend customers deploy mitigations on all instances. Furthermore, the nature of the vulnerability suggests that container escapes are possible, so customers allowing untrusted workloads to execute in their containers may need to take additional steps to secure their containerized workloads.\n\nWe will provide further information regarding our posture and recommended actions for Akamai Compute customers who may be affected. \n\n[1] https://www.akamai.com/legal/security", "incident_id": "msqh44ktjp9g", "created_at": "2026-05-01T17:51:06.734Z", "updated_at": "2026-05-01T17:51:06.734Z", "display_at": "2026-05-01T17:51:06.734Z", "affected_components": [{"code": "v8zpnn61fcdm", "name": "Regions - US-East (Newark)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"}, {"code": "s8355f9s5hpx", "name": "Regions - US-Central (Dallas)", "old_status": "operational", "new_status": "operational"},